interface.longDescription:
GenerApp lets ChatGPT build small web apps for everyday life. Describe what you need, such as a shared shopping list for your flat, a chore rota for the family, a holiday budget split between friends or a small game to play together, and ChatGPT writes the app and publishes it on GenerApp in a few seconds.

Each app gets its own web address. Share the link: everyone opens it in their phone browser and can add it to their home screen like a regular app. The people who use an app need nothing to install and no account.

GenerApp provides what a small app needs: hosting, shared data that syncs in real time between everyone who uses the app, and an optional nickname for each person. ChatGPT only writes the interface; there is no server, database or deployment to set up.

With GenerApp, ChatGPT can:
- create an app, write and read its files, check it and publish it;
- list your apps and update them, keeping the previous version online until the new one is published;
- browse the public library of apps shared by other users and copy one to adapt it;
- show the limits of your account before creating an app.

Each app's data is only visible to people who have its link, and apps shared in the library expose their code, never their data. GenerApp does not call any AI model and does not receive your conversations, only what each tool needs.

A GenerApp account is required; sign in when you connect. The site and the apps are available in English and French.
